{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having some pain in your left arm during dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. It started a few weeks ago. My hand gets cold and tingly when I'm on the machine. It goes away once I'm disconnected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds like steal syndrome. It happens when too much blood flows through your fistula and not enough stays in your hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:19:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if it gets worse. The tissue in your hand might not get enough oxygen. That’s why we’re here—to fix it before that happens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. So what do we do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to do a procedure tomorrow called fistula banding. We’ll slightly narrow the fistula so more blood stays in your hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under anesthesia, so you won’t feel anything during the surgery. Afterward, you might have some soreness, but we’ll manage that with pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I’ve had surgeries before, so I know the drill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll monitor you closely. You’re on dialysis three times a week, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, every Monday, Wednesday, Friday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do dialysis tomorrow after your procedure, just to keep your levels stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. My potassium was high last time—should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:29:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your labs tonight—your potassium is 6.4, which is high, but you’re not having symptoms like muscle weakness or heart issues, so we’re not alarmed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:30:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I didn’t feel different."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:31:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you get a longer dialysis session tomorrow to bring it down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my heart—should I be concerned with the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:33:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have atrial fibrillation and a history of heart issues, so we’ll monitor your rhythm closely. But your heart function is stable, and we’ve cleared you for surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had chest pain before with cocaine, but I haven’t used in years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:35:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that in your history. We’re glad you’re clean now. That helps your overall health a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’m trying to stay on track. This dialysis and everything—it keeps me focused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-01-11 20:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll get you prepped for surgery first thing in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Ready for your procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "As ready as I’ll ever be. Nervous, but I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. The banding was successful. We narrowed the fistula just enough. You’re in recovery now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s awesome. My hand feels normal so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your pulses and sensation—they’re strong and intact. No signs of reduced blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When do I get dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-01-12 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Later this morning. We’ll do a longer session to manage your potassium, which was high yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished dialysis. Everything went smoothly. Your potassium is coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel fine. No cramps or dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your hand still has good color, warmth, and movement. The banding is working as expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I watch for anything after I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Call us if you have increasing pain, numbness, coldness, or if your hand changes color. Also, monitor your weight—call if you gain more than three pounds in a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my meds—should I restart them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:37:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, take all your home medications unless we told you otherwise. Especially your blood pressure, diabetes, and heart meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have insulin and gabapentin for nerve pain—those are fine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:40:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue both. And use the oxycodone every four hours if you need it for pain—don’t wait until it’s severe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:41:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:42:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see the transplant surgery clinic in a few days. They’ll check your fistula and make sure it’s healing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sleep apnea? I forgot my CPAP at the facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:45:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sleep medicine recommends you get re-evaluated. Make sure to follow up with them—good sleep helps your heart and blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll ask the facility to help me set that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:47:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re doing well. We’ll discharge you to your extended care facility today in stable condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:50:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything concerns you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:51:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at the follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:52:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and keep up the good work with your health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-01-12 10:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m trying. One day at a time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-01-11 20:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-01-12 20:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis presented with left arm pain due to worsening steal syndrome in his left brachiocephalic arteriovenous fistula. He underwent elective fistula banding the following day, which was successful in reducing blood flow to alleviate symptoms while preserving access function. He remained asymptomatic postoperatively with no neurovascular deficits. His potassium was elevated at 6.4 on admission but decreased after an extended hemodialysis session. He tolerated a regular diet, maintained baseline functional status, and was discharged in stable condition to an extended care facility. Follow-up was arranged with transplant surgery and sleep medicine. Home medications were resumed, and discharge instructions included monitoring for arm symptoms, weight changes, and dialysis access issues.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "Disturbance of skin sensation",
      "Pain in limb",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
